  <section class="faith-intro">
    <div class="container container-narrow">
      <details class="faith-intro-disclosure" data-faith-intro>
        <summary class="faith-intro-summary">
          <span class="faith-intro-summary-label" data-faith-intro-label>Read introduction</span>
          <span class="faith-intro-summary-chev" aria-hidden="true"></span>
        </summary>
        <div class="faith-intro-body">
          <p class="faith-intro-prose hero-excerpt-dropcap">The Lausanne Covenant was issued by the 1974 International Congress on World Evangelization, convened in Lausanne by Billy Graham and John Stott. Its 15 articles are the founding statement of contemporary global evangelicalism - a confession of biblical authority, a call to evangelism inseparable from social concern, and an explicit repentance for the cultural captivity of Western missions. It remains the closest thing modern evangelical Protestantism has to an ecumenical creed.</p>
        </div>
      </details>
    </div>
  </section>
    
